 "extra": {
  "decision": "Issue #708: the table describes every PF circuit the machine has, not only the five energised in the reference era, so a discharge that energised a different subset needs no new table. nfsum 16 -> 26, nfcoil 302 -> 530, +4.1 MB.",
  "generator": "workflow/efit_tables/regenerate_legacy_table.py",
  "identity_excludes_mhdout": "Issue #793: mhdout.dat is EFUND's echo of its own namelist, carries at least one uninitialised Fortran value (KUBICS came back 83664424 from one run and 4890152 from the next, against an input of 4), and is read by nothing. Its hash stays under table.files; it no longer decides table.identity, so the same inputs now produce the same identity.",
  "incheck_replaced_after_the_run": "Issue #649: the shipped mhdin.dat's &incheck block was replaced with the machine-derived acceptance envelope after this EFUND run, so efund.input.sha256 above describes what built the tables and no longer matches the file as shipped (now sha256 9e09ac3ce7832d322b934e85fcb912ef8908a340c7fdf966e7e9b0aaab90ff9c). EFUND never reads &incheck -- it is read in exactly one place, EFIT's read_namelist.F90 -- so the Green tables are unaffected and were not regenerated. Measured on 39915, this block alone: as shipped every plasma slice was rejected (14 of 14, all on failure #21, the virial delbp); with the derived envelope 10 of 14 are accepted and the rest fail chi-square.",
  "installed_as": "vaft/data/efit",
  "installed_at": "2026-09-15",
  "legacy_mhdin_moved": "The 16-lumped-conductor namelist that used to sit here is at legacy/mhdin.dat. It is no longer loadable as a table directory -- its nfsum is 16 -- and is kept only as the independent reference test_efund_geometry.py checks the canonical geometry against.",
  "seconds": 184.58953304204624,
  "limiter_moved_after_the_run": "Issue #965: both vertical limiter faces moved off EFIT grid lines in VEST_static_geometry.json.gz (wall IDS only) and lim.dat -- inboard R = 0.104 -> 0.105 m and outboard R = 0.760 -> 0.761 m -- because the default grid's columns at R = 0.10391 m and 0.75977 m sat 0.09 mm and 0.23 mm from them; a 0.01 mm inward move of the inboard face flipped 3 of 4 inboard-limited 39915 slices from converged to diverged. Both new positions keep the same 6327-point plasma grid. machine.static_inputs.static_geometry.sha256 above still names the file this EFUND run read; only its wall changed since, and EFUND reads neither the wall nor lim.dat, so the Green tables are unaffected and were not regenerated. The limiter-derived &incheck bounds were re-derived (aminor_max 32.8 unchanged net, rcntr/rcurrt_min +0.1 cm, rcntr/rcurrt_max +0.1 cm)."
 },
